1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:04,459
In five weeks, NVIDIA’s value fell by $1.8 trillion.

2
00:00:04,619 --> 00:00:08,381
That’s almost half of India’s yearly economy, wiped off its share price.

3
00:00:08,381 --> 00:00:08,863
How?

4
00:00:09,023 --> 00:00:11,634
NVIDIA makes the chips AI runs on.

5
00:00:11,634 --> 00:00:14,115
ChatGPT needs thousands of them.

6
00:00:14,275 --> 00:00:19,592
Every tech giant wanted them, so in October NVIDIA hit a record $5.8 trillion.

7
00:00:19,752 --> 00:00:21,349
Then, within weeks, three shocks.

8
00:00:21,509 --> 00:00:26,310
One: US voters passed local rules that could slow new AI data centres.

9
00:00:26,470 --> 00:00:30,325
Two: NVIDIA invests in AI start-ups, who then buy its chips.

10
00:00:30,325 --> 00:00:31,843
Is that real demand?

11
00:00:32,003 --> 00:00:36,286
Three: its CEO, Jensen Huang, stepped down amid a board investigation.

12
00:00:36,446 --> 00:00:37,034
Bubble?

13
00:00:37,034 --> 00:00:38,661
Sales still doubled in a year.

14
00:00:38,661 --> 00:00:40,469
Investors just fear it won’t last.

15
00:00:40,629 --> 00:00:42,513
A share price is a bet on the future.

16
00:00:42,513 --> 00:00:44,266
The bet flipped, not the business.

17
00:00:44,426 --> 00:00:45,942
Follow InvisiTech for more.

